    "tier": "weak",
    "category": "",
    "description": "The architect: small, dark-haired, with folding gold spectacles, always in a purple velour robe, pyjama trousers and slippers inside the hotel. Quiet, sombre, refined and judgemental of those who \"fall below the keel\" of history. Everything in his charge must be just so, to the point of madness: he will run from cover in a gunfight to gather spent cartridges, or stab a ruined corpse on its other side to even it out. He kills the children because the King tells him to.\nStuck: by day he \"repairs\" the hotel and gathers rumours from staff and guests; by night he is in the Drowning Room. He has never found the Labyrinth. Where's my bottle? He would do anything for someone who brings him his bottle, or brings him to it.",
